# crontab - scheduled jobs, output in /var/log/cron.log (see: man cron)
#   @boot <command>              once when the board starts
#   every <N>s|m|h|d <command>   repeatedly, e.g. every 30m
#   at HH:MM <command>           daily (set the clock first: date ntp)
# See the output with: cron log. Reload after editing: cron reload
# Holding BOOTSEL while the board starts skips this whole file.
# Comments only on their own line - a # after a command is not one.

# --- Network services at start (remove the # to use) ---
# Passwords first: conf TELNET_PASS <pw>, conf HTTPD_PASS <pw>
# @boot run /root/program.py start
# @boot wifi -r 5
# @boot date ntp
# @boot telnetd
# @boot httpd

# --- Keep it running ---
# Reconnect if WiFi dropped (does nothing while connected):
# every 5m wifi
# Keep the clock right:
# every 6h date ntp

# --- Logging ---
# Board temperature every 10 min, view: plot -f 2 /root/temp.csv
# every 10m temp | log -n /root/temp.csv

# --- Maintenance ---
# Daily restart for an unattended board (needs the clock set):
# at 04:00 reboot
